# Design Blocks (Blocks network agent)

Before building a new page, screen, or component — or whenever choosing
colors, fonts, or layout — get direction from the `design_blocks` agent via
the blocks-network MCP server:

1. Call the `send_task` MCP tool: agent `design_blocks`, text input `brief`
   = JSON `{goal, vibe, framework, count}` or a plain sentence describing
   what you are about to build and how it should feel.

2. Poll `get_task` until complete. You get `comps` (three rendered comps,
   winner ringed — SHOW THIS to the user), `blueprint` (THE PAGE:
   section-by-section layout with exact sizes/overlaps/rotations),
   `theme_css` + `motion_css` + `motion_js` (styling and micro-animation
   kit), `stickers` (floating SVG components), `kit`, `hero`/`og` PNGs.

3. THE BLUEPRINT IS THE PAGE — build it section by section with its exact
   numbers; it outranks your layout habits. Link theme, then motion css,
   then motion js (defer). Inline sticker SVGs as the blueprint's floating
   elements with data-float; add data-reveal / data-reveal-group where the
   blueprint says. Save hero/og into public/ and wire them.

4. Never: a centered gradient-card hero unless the blueprint says so,
   three identical boxes in a row, shrunken display type, ad-hoc
   keyframes, or emoji as icons. The motion kit is the only animation
   source; the stickers are the produced look — use them.

4. Mention which references were matched so the user can steer — a new
   `vibe` in the next brief re-aims the direction.
